WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:04.910
Stranger Things 3 is without a doubt the big
release for July, but there's plenty more

00:00:04.910 --> 00:00:06.040
to look forward to.

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:11.080
Here's a look at everything good coming to
Netflix in July 2019, starting with the Netflix

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:12.080
originals.

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:16.400
History buffs aren't the only audience for
Netflix's upcoming The Last Czars.

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:21.140
The series will combine documentary-style
information plugs with dramatic reenactments

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:25.070
to trace the history of Czar Nicholas II,
Russia's last emperor.

00:00:25.070 --> 00:00:29.370
Let's put it this way: If your only knowledge
of the Romanovs, the February Revolution,

00:00:29.370 --> 00:00:33.820
and Rasputin comes from watching Anastasia
as a kid, get ready for a whole new world

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:37.879
of insight into the revolution that brought
the Romanov dynasty to its knees.

00:00:37.880 --> 00:00:41.240
Tune in for the entire series when it arrives
on July 3rd.

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:46.280
There probably isn't a single person watching
this who needs a recap of Stranger Things.

00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:51.149
Netflix's throwback horror/fantasy series
took the streaming world by storm in 2016,

00:00:51.149 --> 00:00:54.519
then upped the insanity with Season 2 in 2017.

00:00:54.519 --> 00:00:58.250
It's hard to believe that nearly two years
have passed since we last saw Eleven and her

00:00:58.250 --> 00:01:03.039
friends battle the forces of the Upside Down,
but it looks like the wait was more than worth

00:01:03.039 --> 00:01:09.920
it.

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:14.890
Stranger Things 3 sees the kids a little older,
and hopefully a little wiser, as their hometown

00:01:14.890 --> 00:01:18.960
of Hawkins, Indiana, is once again threatened
by otherworldly beasts.

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:21.840
Take a look when Stranger Things 3 arrives
on July 4th.

00:01:22.120 --> 00:01:25.880
Don't let the subtitles turn you off to Cities
of Last Things.

00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:30.039
If you're a fan of gritty psychological thrillers
like Memento or Jacob's Ladder, you'll have

00:01:30.039 --> 00:01:32.840
a good time watching this dystopian Taiwanese
film.

00:01:32.840 --> 00:01:37.810
Told in reverse chronological order, the story
follows a depressed ex-cop whose life is on

00:01:37.810 --> 00:01:39.270
a downward spiral.

00:01:39.270 --> 00:01:43.310
Beginning with one shocking act, Cities of
Last Things then backtracks over the three

00:01:43.310 --> 00:01:45.659
days leading up to his fateful decision.

00:01:45.659 --> 00:01:47.720
Look for it to hit Netflix on July 11th.

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:52.710
Anthony Mackie takes the lead in Point Blank
as a nurse on the hunt for the criminals who

00:01:52.710 --> 00:01:54.320
kidnapped his pregnant wife.

00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:58.840
To bring the thugs to justice, he'll have
to team up with the suspect of a murder investigation,

00:01:58.840 --> 00:02:01.929
played by Frank Grillo, and descend into the
criminal underworld.

00:02:01.929 --> 00:02:04.030
"Where are you going?

00:02:04.030 --> 00:02:06.130
I'm gonna kill them.

00:02:06.130 --> 00:02:07.710
All of them."

00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:12.200
Point Blank is a remake of the 2011 French
thriller of the same name, and Netflix couldn't

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:14.020
have picked a better source for their film.

00:02:14.020 --> 00:02:18.780
The original garnered a 91 percent approval
rating on Rotten Tomatoes, with critics praising

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:20.880
the sharp action and furious pace.

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:23.600
Look for Point Blank to land on Netflix on
July 12th.

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:28.520
How do you give audiences a fresh take on
the age-old Frankenstein story?

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:33.870
Easy: You do whatever the hell Netflix is
doing with Frankenstein's Monster's Monster,

00:02:33.870 --> 00:02:34.870
Frankenstein.

00:02:34.870 --> 00:02:39.330
Not only is that a tongue twister of a title,
it also looks like a brain twister of a story.

00:02:39.330 --> 00:02:43.640
Stranger Things' David Harbour stars in this
short mockumentary as a man who's digging

00:02:43.640 --> 00:02:48.440
into his father's past to uncover secrets
about an old Frankenstein-themed play.

00:02:48.440 --> 00:02:49.440
What does it all mean?

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:54.730
We'll have to wait until July 16th to find
out, when Frankenstein's Monster's Monster,

00:02:54.730 --> 00:02:56.440
Frankenstein shows up on Netflix.

00:02:56.440 --> 00:03:01.040
Secret Obsession centers on a woman named
Jennifer, played by The Social Network's Brenda

00:03:01.069 --> 00:03:05.270
Song, who wakes up to a headful of amnesia
and a husband who may be keeping dangerous

00:03:05.270 --> 00:03:06.280
secrets from her.

00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:09.250
Mike Vogel co-stars as Jennifer's husband
Russel.

00:03:09.250 --> 00:03:13.200
Netflix has so far only teased the upcoming
film, but all signs point to a tense, edge-of-your-seat

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:14.280
thriller.

00:03:14.280 --> 00:03:16.520
Take a look on July 18th.

00:03:16.520 --> 00:03:21.240
If you're one of the avid watchers of La Casa
de Papel, or Money Heist, you're no doubt

00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:22.959
pumped about the series' return.

00:03:22.959 --> 00:03:27.470
According to Deadline, it's the streaming
service's most popular non-English language

00:03:27.470 --> 00:03:30.650
series, and if you've ever given it a chance
you know that it's worth the hype.

00:03:30.650 --> 00:03:34.660
Even if you haven't tried it, you might still
recognize it as the one with all the people

00:03:34.660 --> 00:03:36.879
in masks and red jumpsuits.

00:03:36.879 --> 00:03:40.909
Without giving too much away, the show basically
involves an elaborate heist on the Spanish

00:03:40.909 --> 00:03:42.290
Royal Mint.

00:03:42.290 --> 00:03:46.860
Originally slated as a limited series in Spain,
Netflix commissioned a third part in early

00:03:46.860 --> 00:03:50.790
2018, most likely due to the overwhelming
popularity of the series.

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:54.900
If this is your first run-in with Money Heist,
you still have plenty of time to catch up

00:03:54.900 --> 00:03:57.560
before Part 3 arrives on July 19th.

00:03:57.560 --> 00:04:02.360
We're not entirely sure what to expect with
this upcoming sci-fi series, but hopefully

00:04:02.379 --> 00:04:05.110
Another Life turns out just as good as it
looks.

00:04:05.110 --> 00:04:09.810
Katee Sackhoff stars as an astronaut who's
leading a crew into space to check out a mysterious

00:04:09.810 --> 00:04:11.230
alien artifact.

00:04:11.230 --> 00:04:15.829
Another Life comes from creator Aaron Martin,
who also created Netflix's horror series Slasher

00:04:15.829 --> 00:04:18.440
- another show worth checking out for horror
fans.

00:04:18.440 --> 00:04:22.440
Take a look at Another Life when the first
season arrives on July 25th.

00:04:22.440 --> 00:04:26.920
Fans who have followed Orange is the New Black
for six seasons are surely getting excited

00:04:26.940 --> 00:04:28.830
about the upcoming series finale.

00:04:28.830 --> 00:04:33.520
Season 7 sees Piper out of prison and trying
to cope with her life in the outside world,

00:04:33.520 --> 00:04:35.680
but finding it tougher than she expected.

00:04:35.680 --> 00:04:39.560
Much of the cast has come forward to shed
a light on their feelings about the series'

00:04:39.560 --> 00:04:42.220
end, with most conceding that it's a bittersweet
finale.

00:04:42.220 --> 00:04:47.080
Tune in for the final season of Orange is
the New Black when it premieres on July 26th.

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:51.870
Netflix is closing out the month with The
Red Sea Diving Resort, a political action

00:04:51.870 --> 00:04:56.560
thriller starring Chris Evans as the leader
of a team working to get Ethiopian refugees

00:04:56.560 --> 00:04:57.560
to safety.

00:04:57.560 --> 00:05:01.870
According to BBC, the premise is based on
a real life resort in Sudan that was set up

00:05:01.870 --> 00:05:03.900
by Mossad agents in the '80s.

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:07.800
It's an intriguing story, and we can't wait
to see what Chris Evans does with the role.

00:05:07.800 --> 00:05:09.620
Look for it on July 31st.

00:05:09.620 --> 00:05:13.930
That covers all the best new Netflix originals
for July; let's pivot now to check out the

00:05:13.930 --> 00:05:15.720
rest of the films heading our way.

00:05:15.800 --> 00:05:20.640
Netflix is clearly focusing the month on its
original films and series, and while there's

00:05:20.650 --> 00:05:25.280
plenty to look forward to there, there aren't
a lot of licensed genre films to look forward

00:05:25.280 --> 00:05:26.280
to.

00:05:26.280 --> 00:05:30.040
Action is taking a real hit, with only four
additions in July, all of which arrive on

00:05:30.040 --> 00:05:31.040
the 1st.

00:05:31.040 --> 00:05:34.009
Fortunately, they're all worth a watch - even
if it's a rewatch.

00:05:34.009 --> 00:05:40.430
1989's Road House is showing up, right beside
2001's Swordfish, 2010's The Book of Eli,

00:05:40.430 --> 00:05:44.160
and 2005's offbeat fantasy adventure comedy
The Brothers Grimm.

00:05:44.160 --> 00:05:47.850
Similarly, there are only three new thriller
additions in the thriller genre.

00:05:47.850 --> 00:05:52.070
Look for 2006's Mean Dreams, which marks Bill
Paxton's final film role.

00:05:52.070 --> 00:05:56.669
Mean Dreams is a dramatic thriller about a
boy named Jonas who sees his father, a corrupt

00:05:56.669 --> 00:05:59.259
police officer, steal a satchel of drug money.

00:05:59.259 --> 00:06:03.020
Jonas takes the money and leaves with his
girlfriend, looking for a better life, but

00:06:03.020 --> 00:06:06.060
it isn't long before his own father begins
hunting him down.

00:06:06.060 --> 00:06:10.900
You can catch Mean Dreams on July 1, along
with everyone's favorite shaky monster movie,

00:06:10.900 --> 00:06:12.660
Cloverfield, and Scream 3.

00:06:12.660 --> 00:06:19.210
"It's your turn to scream, a------."

00:06:19.210 --> 00:06:23.570
On the drama front, Netflix is adding some
of the more obscure, earlier Martin Scorcese

00:06:23.570 --> 00:06:30.560
films, including 1973's Mean Streets, 1974's
Alice Doesn't Live Here Anymore, and 1967's

00:06:30.560 --> 00:06:32.150
Who's That Knocking at My Door?

00:06:32.150 --> 00:06:34.090
All of those arrive on July 1st.

00:06:34.090 --> 00:06:38.260
Other additions on the first of the month
include Oscar winners Rain Man and Philadelphia,

00:06:38.260 --> 00:06:41.139
with 2011's The Iron Lady coming on the 6th.

00:06:41.139 --> 00:06:45.110
Finally, close out the month with Quentin
Tarantino's World War II opus Inglourious

00:06:45.110 --> 00:06:46.960
Basterds on the 22nd.

00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:51.479
Notable comedy additions include both Caddyshack
films, The Hangover, and the two Pink Panther

00:06:51.479 --> 00:06:54.169
reboot films, if you're into that kind of
thing.

00:06:54.169 --> 00:06:56.150
Those all show up on the first.

00:06:56.150 --> 00:06:58.370
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:06:58.370 --> 00:07:02.250
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
Netflix shows are coming soon.

00:07:02.250 --> 00:07:05.729
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

